op_lab_safety_replay","requirements_review":{"status":"unrecorded"},"summary":"This validator reads synthetic candidate, simulator assay, safety-screen, and selection records.","title":"Materials Chemistry Simulator Safety Replay"},"claim_ceiling":"artifact safety/refusal validation only, not wetlab execution, materials discovery, robot command, live assay, release, benchmark, or provider authority","claim_ceiling_restated":"Recomputes the selected candidate from synthetic assay, active-learning and safety-gate scores and compares it with the declared selection, rejecting cases such as wet-lab protocol steps or a discovery claim.","claim_id":"claim::materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay","evidence_class":"algorithmic_projection","evidence_strength_rank":3,"organ_id":"materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay","truth_accounting_bucket":"source_faithful_refactor","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay run --input fixtures/first_wave/materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay/input --out receipts/first_wave/materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay --acceptance-out receipts/acceptance/first_wave/materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay_fixture_acceptance.json"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"55eb540ed0c098ae017351accf9e2c31383acdb814999c5e0e0194b1de05b3cb","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"algorithmic_projection","family":"research_and_science_replays","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"source_faithful_refactor"},"component_id":"materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay","plain":"When software picks which material a lab should test next, someone should check that the pick follows from the scores. This component reads made-up records of candidate materials, simulated lab tests, safety screening and the candidate declared as chosen. It works out the pick again from a stand-in test score, a score for what to test next and a safety score, then compares it with the declared pick. It writes a result with findings and rejects a pick that no longer matches the scores or a claimed hands-on lab procedure.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay.md","sha256":"10c2f88ced5df29eb4b46d1d4a1a214ec40244080828b7c24e1c7a1de6808914","text":"# Materials Chemistry Simulator Safety Replay\n\n> **In plain terms.** When software picks which material a lab should test next, someone should check that the pick follows from the scores. This component reads made-up records of candidate materials, simulated lab tests, safety screening and the candidate declared as chosen. It works out the pick again from a stand-in test score, a score for what to test next and a safety score, then compares it with the declared pick. It writes a result with findings and rejects a pick that no longer matches the scores or a claimed hands-on lab procedure.\n\nThis validator reads synthetic candidate, simulator assay, safety-screen, and selection records. It recomputes the selected candidate using assay proxy, active-learning, and safety-gate scores, then compares the result with the declared selection. It also checks the replay graph, source manifests, and negative-case refusals before writing a result and board.\n\nThe fixture rejects a claimed wet-lab procedure and the tests reject a stale selection after scores change. The result concerns the supplied simulated records; it does not run an experiment or robot, establish laboratory safety, or demonstrate a materials discovery. A source digest verifies the referenced copy, not its scientific validity.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root with Python 3.11 or newer, run the supplied fixture into ignored local output:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay run \\\n  --input fixtures/first_wave/materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay/input \\\n  --out .microcosm/component-guides/materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay/out \\\n  --acceptance-out .microcosm/component-guides/materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay/acceptance.json\n```\n\nThe supplied fixture prints `pass` when its simulation records and expected refusals meet the checks.\n\n## Verification\n\nTests exercise the synthetic scoring and refusal cases; they do not formally prove the scoring algorithm. `make component-replays` runs the exported lab bundle through the [shared Dafny admission check](../formal/replay/README.md) for agreement among supplied source, input, claim policy and receipt observations. The direct command does not invoke that gate.\n\n## Source and evidence\n\n- [Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay.py) and [fixture inputs](../fixtures/first_wave/materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay/input/).\n- [Tests](../tests/test_materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay.py).\n- [Saved example result](../receipts/first_wave/materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay/materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay_result.json) (historical, not a fresh run).\n- [Component JSON record](./materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay.json) and [canonical capsule](../core/paper_module_capsules.json).\n"},"proofs":[],"replay":{"command":"make component-replays","command_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_replays.py","command_scope":"all registered components","configuration_refs":["s